Source: minti-pack-fetch
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: MINTI Project <minti@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: minti-pack-fetch
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
 ollama
Description: MINTI addon-pack content fetcher
 Single-binary helper that reads /usr/share/minti/packs/<name>/manifest.json
 and dispatches by `kind`:
 .
   * ollama-model — shells to `ollama pull <tag>` (idempotent).
   * kiwix-zim    — HTTPS Range-resumable download with SHA-256 verify and
                    1.25x free-disk precheck, then atomic rename.
 .
 Writes /var/lib/minti/packs/<name>.installed state markers (consumed by
 minti-fetch's `Addons:` line). Honours MINTI_PACK_NO_FETCH=1: writes the
 marker without downloading, so `apt install minti-pack-<addon>` finishes
 fast on a slow link and the operator runs `sudo minti-pack-fetch <name>`
 later when bandwidth and disk allow.
 .
 Required by all MINTI addon packs (minti-pack-hermes3, minti-pack-mistral,
 minti-pack-wiki-simple, ...).
 .
 Ships a pre-built Go binary (compiled by `make pack-fetch-linux` on the
 host or in CI) rather than rebuilding at dpkg-buildpackage time — keeps
 the build dep-list to just debhelper and matches the project convention
 (cland, runtime, MCP servers all package pre-built artifacts the same way).
 .
 Installs the binary at /usr/bin/minti-pack-fetch. (install.sh continues to
 deploy a bare binary at /usr/local/bin/minti-pack-fetch for operators who
 don't install via dpkg; PATH lookup finds either one.)
